WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:08.890
Last week's sit down with Brigitte Gabriel
received quite possibly the most positive

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:11.560
reaction we've ever had to an interview.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:17.189
I'd say well over 90% of the responses that
I saw on YouTube, Twitter and Facebook were

00:00:17.189 --> 00:00:21.840
appreciative off our discussion of her incredible
story growing up in Lebanon during the civil

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.980
war, about the roots of radical Islam, and
what living in a free society is really all

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.080
about.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.239
People were in awe of Brigitte's personal
story, amazed by her passion, impressed by

00:00:32.239 --> 00:00:35.370
her candor, or some combination thereof.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.700
If you haven't seen her episode yet, but you
only have a few minutes, just check out the

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:45.540
last 5 minutes of our chat to see what true
love of freedom and liberty is all about.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.570
We'll put the link to that right here in the
description.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:53.830
And, for the record, I wasn't tearing up because
of her impassioned speech, it was these damn

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.809
bright lights were getting to me!

00:00:55.809 --> 00:00:57.960
Yes, yes, that's it, these damned bright lights.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.320
I mention the reaction to our interview with
Brigitte because it reiterates a lesson I've

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:05.100
consistently learned by doing this show.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.340
Before we had Brigitte on, I talked to my
team about whether we should have her on at

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:10.340
all.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:15.680
After all, Brigitte is hated by a lot of people
who call her the usual buzzwords like racist,

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.510
bigot, far right extremist, and so on.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:23.610
While we all know the people who are using
these words are becoming the new boy who cried

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:28.420
wolf, and these words themselves are losing
their meaning by the minute, the chill effect

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.320
these words have still remains in certain
quarters.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.990
Even in my case, when I'm selecting guests,
I do have to think for a moment if there's

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:40.600
going to be some sort of cost for me to sit
down with someone.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:45.720
I still get plenty of hate for talking to
Milo, Mike Cernovich, Tommy Robinson, Paul

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.440
Joseph Watson and some others.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:54.260
In none of those cases do I regret having
the conversations, regardless of the blowback

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:59.350
these interviews may have caused me, but it
does bring to light an important topic.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:04.650
It's not just those who are being targeted
as bigots and racists who are in the firing

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.220
line of those who would like to silence us.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:11.409
It's also the people willing to talk to those
people and hear them out.

00:02:11.409 --> 00:02:16.560
This guilt by association is incredibly dangerous
because it can bite any of us for having a

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.569
family member, or even a friendship, with
someone who shares political views that fall

00:02:21.569 --> 00:02:22.969
out of the mainstream.

00:02:22.969 --> 00:02:26.150
Should we disown people with views different
than ours?

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.150
Defame them?

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:29.150
Publicly humiliate them?

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:34.670
All of these are small steps towards reporting
them to the authorities for wrongthink.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:40.150
We should also note in the online word, there
is an information battle constantly happening.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:45.879
When you put Brigitte's name in Google, the
first site that comes up which isn't one of

00:02:45.879 --> 00:02:53.879
her own is to islamophobia.org, which is part
of CAIR, the council on American Islamic Relations.

00:02:53.879 --> 00:02:56.859
Now think back to my interview with Brigitte.

00:02:56.859 --> 00:02:58.470
What was the bigoted part?

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:03.340
After living through everything she has, does
she strike you as the problem in society?

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:08.840
Does she strike you as a bigot or a racist
or a right wing nut?

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:12.720
What I think is most interesting about the
assault on conversation is how recent this

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:13.959
phenomenon is.

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:18.180
My friend and mentor Larry King has built
his legendary career on talking to people

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.280
from every walk of life and from every part
of the world.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:26.420
On 5 days of any given week he could talk
to a member of the Ku Klux Klan, then Louis

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:31.110
Farrakhan, then the cast of Friends, then
Magic Johnson and then the Pope.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:35.902
Nobody ever accused him of sharing all of
their beliefs just because he talked to all

00:03:35.902 --> 00:03:36.902
of them.

00:03:36.902 --> 00:03:40.409
Actually, this very concept would've been
totally ludicrous.

00:03:40.409 --> 00:03:44.489
I'm proud to say that I know Larry pretty
well, and it's his curious mind and real sense

00:03:44.489 --> 00:03:50.060
of wonder that made and still make him want
to talk to all sorts of people doing all sorts

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.569
of different things.

00:03:51.569 --> 00:03:56.559
As you know my policy is that sunlight is
the best disinfectant -- people with bad ideas

00:03:56.559 --> 00:04:02.799
will eventually hang themselves if given even
room to do so, which I always try to do.

00:04:02.799 --> 00:04:07.409
This growing sense of guilt by association
is just the next level of what the Regressive

00:04:07.409 --> 00:04:09.129
Left has done.

00:04:09.129 --> 00:04:13.909
It's not enough to just label someone a bigot
anymore, now we have to tar and feather them

00:04:13.909 --> 00:04:17.840
so other people will be afraid to talk to
them as well.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.720
And if you're willing to talk to someone out
of their accepted group, they'll tar and feather

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:26.430
you as well to shut down any furthering of
the conversation.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:33.330
And yes, unfortunately, I do see this phenomenon
far more on the left than on the right.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:37.390
It's almost as if when you cut through the
hysteria and screaming and slandering they

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:40.870
don't even believe their own ideas.

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:45.260
So they don't want counter ideas heard, but
they also want to make sure people aren't

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.820
entertaining other ideas in the first place.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:52.710
This is incredibly dangerous and it's not
a game that I'll be taking part of.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:57.350
We can't give them an inch because they will
keep taking and taking until there is nothing

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:58.410
of us left.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:02.900
Between this silencing of those who veer from
the mainstream and the YouTube demonetization

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:07.030
I discuss last week, those of us who really
are fighting for free speech have our work

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:10.710
cut out for us.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:14.900
Fortunately, we're continuing out partnership
with Learn Liberty this week and joining me

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:19.490
is assistant professor of economics at the
University of Tampa Abby Hall.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:25.400
Abby is also a affiliates scholar at the Mercatus
Institute and a research fellow with the Independent

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:28.730
Institute, a non partisan educational think
tank.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:33.710
We're going to talk economics, war and peace,
the drug war, our militarized police and much

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:34.710
more.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:39.940
I'll gladly accept my guilt by association
to her, and we'll see how it goes as to whether

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.870
she can say the same about me.

